[8.881561, "o", "# docshare API\r\n\r\ndocshare serves the documents that the ingest worker stores in its SQLite database (uploads go through the ingest\r\nworker, not this API). Who may call what is in `PERMISSIONS.md`.\r\n\r\n## Running it\r\n```\r\npython -m docshare.serve --db <path to the SQLite file> --port <port>\r\n```\r\nThe service listens on 127.0.0.1, uses the database file given by `--db` (it must exist; the service never creates\r\none) and keeps all its state there. `python -m docshare.seed --out <path>` builds a fresh development database.\r\n\r\n## Conventions\r\n- Logged-in requests send `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; `X-Org-Id: <organisation id>` chooses the active\r\n  organisation (`PERMISSIONS.md` section 2).\r\n- Request and response bodies are JSON unless stated. Errors are JSON `{\"error\": \"<code>\"}`.\r\n- Ids are UUID strings. Times are ISO 8601 strings in UTC, for example `2026-09-14T10:22:05Z`.\r\n\r\n## Objects\r\n**File**: `id`, `org_id`, `folder_id`, `name`, `mime_type`, `size` (bytes, integer), `uploaded_by` (user id),\r\n`created_a"]
[8.881635, "o", "t`.\r\n\r\n**Folder**: `id`, `org_id`, `name`.\r\n\r\n## Endpoints\r\n| Method and path | Success | Body of a successful response |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| `GET /api/health` | 200 | `{\"ok\": true}`; no login |\r\n| `GET /api/me` | 200 | `{\"user\": {\"id\", \"email\", \"name\", \"is_support\"}, \"active_org_id\", \"role\", \"memberships\": [{\"org_id\", \"role\"}]}`; `active_org_id` is `null` and `role` is `\"support\"` for support without `X-Org-Id` |\r\n| `GET /api/files` | 200 | `{\"files\": [File, ...]}`: the files of the active organisation, sorted by name |\r\n| `GET /api/folders` | 200 | `{\"folders\": [Folder, ...]}`: the folders of the active organisation, sorted by name |\r\n| `GET /api/folders/<folder_id>/files` | 200 | `{\"folder\": Folder, \"files\": [File, ...]}`, files sorted by name |\r\n| `GET /api/files/<file_id>` | 200 | File |\r\n| `GET /api/files/<file_id>/download` | 200 | the file's bytes, with its `mime_type` as Content-Type and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=\"<name>\"` |\r\n| `GET /api/files/<file_id>/thumb` | 200 | an `image/svg+xml"]
[8.881677, "o", "` preview: the file name and the first lines of a text file |\r\n| `PATCH /api/files/<file_id>` with `{\"name\": \"<new name>\"}` | 200 | the updated File; the name must be 1 to 200 characters without `/`, else `400` |\r\n| `DELETE /api/files/<file_id>` | 204 | empty; the file and its share links are removed |\r\n| `POST /api/files/<file_id>/shares` | 201 | `{\"token\", \"url\", \"file_id\", \"created_at\"}`; `url` is `/s/<token>` |\r\n| `DELETE /api/shares/<token>` | 204 | empty; the link stops working |\r\n| `GET /s/<token>` | 200 | the file's bytes, like download; no login |\r\n| `POST /api/export` with `{\"file_ids\": [<id>, ...]}` (1 to 50 ids) | 200 | `{\"files\": [{\"id\", \"name\", \"mime_type\", \"size\", \"content_b64\"}, ...]}` in request order; `content_b64` is the file's bytes in standard base64 |\r\n| `GET /api/admin/orgs` | 200 | `{\"orgs\": [{\"id\", \"name\", \"file_count\"}, ...]}` sorted by name |\r\n\r\nMalformed bodies (for example a missing `name`, or `file_ids` that is not a list of 1 to 50 strings) get `400`.\r\n\r\n## Database\r\nThe schema "]
[8.881704, "o", "is in `docshare/db.py` (`SCHEMA`). Tables: `orgs`, `users`, `memberships`, `folders`, `files` (contents\r\nare stored in `files.content`), `shares` (`revoked_at` is set when a link is revoked).\r\n"]
[8.881836, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[8.881868, "o", "root@d4ccd7b6-ea4d-48a5-a845-5e95f7dffe6e:/app# "]
[9.214142, "i", "for f in docshare/auth.py docshare/db.py docshare/app.py docshare/serve.py docshare/routes/__init__.py docshare/routes/files.py docshare/routes/folders.py docshare/routes/thumbs.py docshare/routes/export.py docshare/routes/share.py docshare/routes/admin.py; do echo \"===== $f =====\"; sed -n '1,320p' \"$f\"; done\n"]
[9.2168, "o", "for f in docshare/auth.py docshare/db.py docshare/app.py docshare/serve.py docshare/routes/__init__.py docshare/routes/files.py docshare/routes/folders.py docshare/routes/thumbs.py docshare/routes/export.py docshare/routes/share.py docshare/routes/admin.py; do echo \"===== $f =====\"; sed -n '1,320p' \"$f\"; done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[9.216952, "o", "===== docshare/auth.py =====\r\n"]
[9.218687, "o", "\"\"\"Who is calling: bearer token -> user, plus the active organisation for this request.\"\"\"\r\nimport functools\r\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\r\n\r\nfrom flask import g, jsonify, request\r\n\r\nfrom . import db\r\n\r\n\r\n@dataclass\r\nclass Identity:\r\n    user_id: str\r\n    email: str\r\n    name: str\r\n    is_support: bool\r\n    org_id: str | None          # the active organisation for this request\r\n    role: str                   # \"member\", \"org_admin\" or \"support\"\r\n    memberships: dict = field(default_factory=dict)   # org_id -> role\r\n\r\n"]
[9.218741, "o", "\r\ndef _bearer_token():\r\n    header = request.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\")\r\n    if not header.startswith(\"Bearer \"):\r\n        return None\r\n    return header[len(\"Bearer \"):].strip() or None\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[9.218787, "o", "def load_identity():\r\n    token = _bearer_token()\r\n    if token is None:\r\n        return None\r\n    user = db.query_one(\"SELECT id, email, name, home_org_id, is_support FROM users WHERE token = ?\", (token,))\r\n    if user is None:\r\n        return None\r\n    memberships = {r[\"org_id\"]: r[\"role\"] for r in\r\n                   db.query_all(\"SELECT org_id, role FROM memberships WHERE user_id = ?\", (user[\"id\"],))}\r\n    # The web client only offers organisations listed by /api/me, so the header names one of the user's orgs.\r\n    org_id = request.headers.get(\"X-Org-Id\") or user[\"home_org_id\"]\r\n    if user[\"is_support\"]:\r\n        role = \"support\"\r\n    else:\r\n        role = memberships.get(org_id, \"member\")\r\n    return Identity(user_id=user[\"id\"], email=user[\"email\"], name=user[\"name\"], is_support=bool(user[\"is_support\"]),\r\n                    org_id=org_id, role=role, memberships=memberships)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef login_required(view):\r\n    @functools.wraps(view)\r\n    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\r\n        ident = load_identity()\r\n"]
[9.218831, "o", "        if ident is None:\r\n            return jsonify(error=\"unauthorized\"), 401\r\n        g.identity = ident\r\n        return view(*args, **kwargs)\r\n    return wrapper\r\n\r\n\r\ndef require_active_org():\r\n    \"\"\"The active organisation id; support must name one with X-Org-Id before listing anything.\"\"\"\r\n    org_id = g.identity.org_id\r\n    if org_id is None:\r\n        from flask import abort\r\n        abort(400, description=\"x_org_id_required\")\r\n    return org_id\r\n"]
[9.219059, "o", "===== docshare/db.py =====\r\n"]
[9.220409, "o", "\"\"\"SQLite access. One connection per request (see app.py); rows come back as sqlite3.Row.\"\"\"\r\nimport sqlite3\r\n\r\nfrom flask import g\r\n\r\nSCHEMA = \"\"\"\r\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS orgs (\r\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\r\n"]
[9.220452, "o", "    name TEXT NOT NULL\r\n);\r\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (\r\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\r\n    email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\r\n    name TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    token TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\r\n"]
[9.220491, "o", "    home_org_id TEXT REFERENCES orgs(id),\r\n    is_support INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0\r\n);\r\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS memberships (\r\n    user_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\r\n    org_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES orgs(id),\r\n    role TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (role IN ('member', 'org_admin')),\r\n    PRIMARY KEY (user_id, org_id)\r\n);\r\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS folders (\r\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\r\n    org_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES orgs(id),\r\n    name TEXT NOT NULL\r\n);\r\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS files (\r\n    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\r\n    org_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES orgs(id),\r\n    folder_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES folders(id),\r\n    name TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n"]
[9.220542, "o", "    mime_type TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    size INTEGER NOT NULL,\r\n    content BLOB NOT NULL,\r\n    uploaded_by TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\r\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\r\n);\r\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS shares (\r\n    token TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\r\n    file_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES files(id),\r\n    created_by TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id),\r\n    created_at TEXT NOT NULL,\r\n    revoked_at TEXT\r\n);\r\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS files_org ON files(org_id, name);\r\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS files_folder ON files(folder_id, name);\r\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS shares_file ON shares(file_id);\r\n"]
[9.220607, "o", "\"\"\"\r\n\r\nFILE_COLUMNS = \"id, org_id, folder_id, name, mime_type, size, uploaded_by, created_at\"\r\n\r\n\r\ndef connect(path):\r\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(path, timeout=10)\r\n    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\r\n    conn.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON\")\r\n    conn.execute(\"PRAGMA busy_timeout = 10000\")\r\n    return conn\r\n\r\n\r\ndef get_db():\r\n    if \"db\" not in g:\r\n        from flask import current_app\r\n        g.db = connect(current_app.config[\"DB_PATH\"])\r\n    return g.db\r\n\r\n\r\ndef close_db(_exc=None):\r\n    conn = g.pop(\"db\", None)\r\n    if conn is not None:\r\n        conn.close()\r\n"]
[9.220649, "o", "\r\n\r\ndef query_one(sql, params=()):\r\n    return get_db().execute(sql, params).fetchone()\r\n\r\n\r\ndef query_all(sql, params=()):\r\n    return get_db().execute(sql, params).fetchall()\r\n\r\n\r\ndef execute(sql, params=()):\r\n    conn = get_db()\r\n    cur = conn.execute(sql, params)\r\n    conn.commit()\r\n    return cur.rowcount\r\n\r\n\r\ndef file_json(row):\r\n    return {\"id\": row[\"id\"], \"org_id\": row[\"org_id\"], \"folder_id\": row[\"folder_id\"], \"name\": row[\"name\"],\r\n            \"mime_type\": row[\"mime_type\"], \"size\": row[\"size\"], \"uploaded_by\": row[\"uploaded_by\"],\r\n            \"created_at\": row[\"created_at\"]}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef folder_json(row):\r\n    return {\"id\": row[\"id\"], \"org_id\": row[\"org_id\"], \"name\": row[\"name\"]}\r\n"]
[9.22085, "o", "===== docshare/app.py =====\r\n"]
[9.222159, "o", "\"\"\"Flask application factory.\"\"\"\r\nfrom flask import Flask, g, jsonify\r\nfrom werkzeug.exceptions import HTTPException\r\n\r\nfrom . import db\r\nfrom .auth import login_required\r\nfrom .routes import admin, export, files, folders, share, thumbs\r\n\r\n\r\ndef create_app(db_path):\r\n    app = Flask(__name__)\r\n    app.config[\"DB_PATH\"] = db_path\r\n"]
[9.222253, "o", "    app.teardown_appcontext(db.close_db)\r\n    for module in (files, folders, thumbs, export, share, admin):\r\n        app.register_blueprint(module.bp)\r\n\r\n    @app.errorhandler(HTTPException)\r\n    def http_error(exc):\r\n        code = exc.description if exc.code == 400 and exc.description and \" \" not in exc.description else exc.name\r\n        return jsonify(error=code.lower().replace(\" \", \"_\")), exc.code\r\n\r\n    @app.get(\"/api/health\")\r\n    def health():\r\n        return jsonify(ok=True)\r\n\r\n    @app.get(\"/api/me\")\r\n    @login_required\r\n    def me():\r\n        ident = g.identity\r\n        return jsonify(user={\"id\": ident.user_id, \"email\": ident.email, \"name\": ident.name,\r\n                             \"is_support\": ident.is_support},\r\n                       active_org_id=ident.org_id, role=ident.role,\r\n                       memberships=[{\"org_id\": o, \"role\": r} for o, r in sorted(ident.memberships.items())])\r\n\r\n    return app\r\n"]
[9.222428, "o", "===== docshare/serve.py =====\r\n"]
[9.223878, "o", "\"\"\"Run the API: python -m docshare.serve --db <path> --port <port>.\"\"\"\r\nimport argparse\r\nimport os\r\nimport sys\r\n\r\nfrom waitress import serve\r\n\r\nfrom . import db\r\nfrom .app import create_app\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[9.223935, "o", "def main(argv=None):\r\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"docshare API server\")\r\n    p.add_argument(\"--db\", required=True, help=\"path to an existing docshare SQLite database\")\r\n    p.add_argument(\"--port\", type=int, default=8080)\r\n    p.add_argument(\"--host\", default=\"127.0.0.1\")\r\n    p.add_argument(\"--threads\", type=int, default=4)\r\n    args = p.parse_args(argv)\r\n    if not os.path.isfile(args.db):\r\n        sys.exit(f\"database not found: {args.db}\")\r\n    conn = db.connect(args.db)\r\n    conn.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL\")\r\n    conn.close()\r\n    serve(create_app(os.path.abspath(args.db)), host=args.host, port=args.port, threads=args.threads,\r\n          ident=\"docshare\")\r\n"]
[9.224018, "o", "\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\n"]
[9.224135, "o", "===== docshare/routes/__init__.py =====\r\n"]
[9.225627, "o", "===== docshare/routes/files.py =====\r\n"]
[9.226846, "o", "\"\"\"File endpoints: list, metadata, download, rename, delete.\"\"\"\r\nfrom flask import Blueprint, Response, abort, g, jsonify, request\r\n\r\nfrom .. import db\r\nfrom ..auth import login_required, require_active_org\r\n\r\nbp = Blueprint(\"files\", __name__)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef get_file_or_404(file_id):\r\n"]
[9.22693, "o", "    row = db.query_one(f\"SELECT {db.FILE_COLUMNS}, content FROM files WHERE id = ?\", (file_id,))\r\n    if row is None:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n    return row\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/api/files\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef list_files():\r\n    org_id = require_active_org()\r\n    rows = db.query_all(f\"SELECT {db.FILE_COLUMNS} FROM files WHERE org_id = ? ORDER BY name\", (org_id,))\r\n    return jsonify(files=[db.file_json(r) for r in rows])\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/api/files/<file_id>\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef get_file(file_id):\r\n    return jsonify(db.file_json(get_file_or_404(file_id)))\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/api/files/<file_id>/download\")\r\n@login_required\r\n"]
[9.226978, "o", "def download(file_id):\r\n    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\r\n    return file_response(row)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef file_response(row):\r\n    resp = Response(bytes(row[\"content\"]), mimetype=row[\"mime_type\"])\r\n    resp.headers[\"Content-Disposition\"] = f'attachment; filename=\"{row[\"name\"]}\"'\r\n    return resp\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.patch(\"/api/files/<file_id>\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef rename(file_id):\r\n    if g.identity.role not in (\"member\", \"org_admin\"):\r\n        abort(403)\r\n    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\r\n    body = request.get_json(silent=True) or {}\r\n    name = body.get(\"name\")\r\n    if not isinstance(name, str) or not (1 <= len(name) <= 200) or \"/\" in name:\r\n        abort(400, description=\"bad_name\")\r\n    db.execute(\"UPDATE files SET name = ? WHERE id = ?\", (name, row[\"id\"]))\r\n    return jsonify(db.file_json(get_file_or_404(row[\"id\"])))\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.delete(\"/api/files/<file_id>\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef delete(file_id):\r\n    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\r\n    conn = db.get_db()\r\n    conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM shares WHERE file_id = ?\", (row[\""]
[9.227017, "o", "id\"],))\r\n    conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM files WHERE id = ?\", (row[\"id\"],))\r\n    conn.commit()\r\n    return \"\", 204\r\n"]
[9.227214, "o", "===== docshare/routes/folders.py =====\r\n"]
[9.228578, "o", "\"\"\"Folder endpoints: the folders of the active organisation and their files.\"\"\"\r\nfrom flask import Blueprint, abort, jsonify\r\n\r\nfrom .. import db\r\nfrom ..auth import login_required, require_active_org\r\n\r\nbp = Blueprint(\"folders\", __name__)\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[9.228618, "o", "@bp.get(\"/api/folders\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef list_folders():\r\n    org_id = require_active_org()\r\n    rows = db.query_all(\"SELECT id, org_id, name FROM folders WHERE org_id = ? ORDER BY name\", (org_id,))\r\n    return jsonify(folders=[db.folder_json(r) for r in rows])\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/api/folders/<folder_id>/files\")\r\n"]
[9.228655, "o", "@login_required\r\ndef folder_files(folder_id):\r\n    org_id = require_active_org()\r\n    folder = db.query_one(\"SELECT id, org_id, name FROM folders WHERE id = ? AND org_id = ?\", (folder_id, org_id))\r\n    if folder is None:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n    rows = db.query_all(f\"SELECT {db.FILE_COLUMNS} FROM files WHERE folder_id = ? AND org_id = ? ORDER BY name\",\r\n                        (folder_id, org_id))\r\n    return jsonify(folder=db.folder_json(folder), files=[db.file_json(r) for r in rows])\r\n"]
[9.228863, "o", "===== docshare/routes/thumbs.py =====\r\n"]
[9.230319, "o", "\"\"\"SVG previews for the file grid.\"\"\"\r\nimport html\r\n\r\nfrom flask import Blueprint, Response, abort\r\n\r\nfrom .. import db\r\nfrom ..auth import login_required\r\n\r\nbp = Blueprint(\"thumbs\", __name__)\r\n\r\nTEXT_TYPES = (\"text/\", \"application/json\")\r\n\r\n"]
[9.230391, "o", "\r\ndef render_thumb(name, mime_type, content):\r\n    lines = []\r\n    if mime_type.startswith(TEXT_TYPES):\r\n        text = bytes(content).decode(\"utf-8\", \"replace\")\r\n        lines = [ln.strip() for ln in text.splitlines() if ln.strip()][:5]\r\n    parts = ['<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"160\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 160 200\">',\r\n             f\"<title>{html.escape(name)}</title>\",\r\n             '<rect x=\"0.5\" y=\"0.5\" width=\"159\" height=\"199\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c8ccd2\"/>',\r\n             f'<text x=\"8\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"bold\">{html.escape(name[:30])}</text>']"]
[9.230434, "o", "\r\n    for i, ln in enumerate(lines):\r\n        parts.append(f'<text x=\"8\" y=\"{40 + 14 * i}\" font-size=\"8\">{html.escape(ln[:34])}</text>')\r\n    parts.append(\"</svg>\")\r\n    return \"\\n\".join(parts)\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/api/files/<file_id>/thumb\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef thumb(file_id):\r\n    row = db.query_one(\"SELECT name, mime_type, content FROM files WHERE id = ?\", (file_id,))\r\n    if row is None:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n    svg = render_thumb(row[\"name\"], row[\"mime_type\"], row[\"content\"])\r\n    return Response(svg, mimetype=\"image/svg+xml\")\r\n"]
[9.230618, "o", "===== docshare/routes/export.py =====\r\n"]
[9.232016, "o", "\"\"\"Bulk export: several files in one JSON response (used by the \"Download selected\" button).\"\"\"\r\nimport base64\r\n\r\nfrom flask import Blueprint, abort, g, jsonify, request\r\n\r\nfrom .. import db\r\nfrom ..auth import login_required\r\n\r\nbp = Blueprint(\"export\", __name__)\r\n\r\nMAX_IDS = 50\r\n"]
[9.232096, "o", "\r\n\r\n@bp.post(\"/api/export\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef export():\r\n    body = request.get_json(silent=True) or {}\r\n    ids = body.get(\"file_ids\")\r\n    if not isinstance(ids, list) or not (1 <= len(ids) <= MAX_IDS) or not all(isinstance(i, str) for i in ids):\r\n        abort(400, description=\"bad_file_ids\")\r\n    # A selection always comes from one folder view, so the first file tells us whose files these are.\r\n    first = db.query_one(\"SELECT org_id FROM files WHERE id = ?\", (ids[0],))\r\n    if first is None:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n    if not g.identity.is_support and first[\"org_id\"] != g.identity.org_id:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n    out = []\r\n    for file_id in ids:\r\n        row = db.query_one(\"SELECT id, name, mime_type, size, content FROM files WHERE id = ?\", (file_id,))\r\n        if row is None:\r\n            abort(404)\r\n        out.append({\"id\": row[\"id\"], \"name\": row[\"name\"], \"mime_type\": row[\"mime_type\"], \"size\": row[\"size\"],\r\n                    \"content_b64\": base64.b64encode(bytes(row[\"content\"])).decode(\"ascii\")})\r"]
[9.232139, "o", "\n    return jsonify(files=out)\r\n"]
[9.232279, "o", "===== docshare/routes/share.py =====\r\n"]
[9.233676, "o", "\"\"\"Share links: create, revoke, and the public download behind /s/<token>.\"\"\"\r\nimport secrets\r\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\r\n\r\nfrom flask import Blueprint, abort, g, jsonify\r\n\r\nfrom .. import db\r\nfrom ..auth import login_required\r\nfrom .files import file_response\r\n\r\n"]
[9.233717, "o", "bp = Blueprint(\"share\", __name__)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef now_iso():\r\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.post(\"/api/files/<file_id>/shares\")\r\n@login_required\r\n"]
[9.233755, "o", "def create_share(file_id):\r\n    if g.identity.role not in (\"member\", \"org_admin\"):\r\n        abort(403)\r\n    row = db.query_one(\"SELECT id FROM files WHERE id = ?\", (file_id,))\r\n    if row is None:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n    token = secrets.token_urlsafe(18)\r\n    created = now_iso()\r\n    db.execute(\"INSERT INTO shares (token, file_id, created_by, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\",\r\n               (token, row[\"id\"], g.identity.user_id, created))\r\n    return jsonify(token=token, url=f\"/s/{token}\", file_id=row[\"id\"], created_at=created), 201\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.delete(\"/api/shares/<token>\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef revoke_share(token):\r\n"]
[9.233796, "o", "    row = db.query_one(\"SELECT s.token, f.org_id FROM shares s JOIN files f ON f.id = s.file_id WHERE s.token = ?\",\r\n                       (token,))\r\n    if row is None or row[\"org_id\"] != g.identity.org_id or g.identity.role not in (\"member\", \"org_admin\"):\r\n        abort(404)\r\n    db.execute(\"UPDATE shares SET revoked_at = ? WHERE token = ? AND revoked_at IS NULL\", (now_iso(), token))\r\n    return \"\", 204\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/s/<token>\")\r\ndef public_download(token):\r\n    row = db.query_one(\"SELECT f.id, f.name, f.mime_type, f.content FROM shares s JOIN files f ON f.id = s.file_id \"\r\n                       \"WHERE s.token = ? AND s.revoked_at IS NULL\", (token,))\r\n    if row is None:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n    return file_response(row)\r\n"]
[9.234, "o", "===== docshare/routes/admin.py =====\r\n"]
[9.235415, "o", "\"\"\"Support console: an overview of every organisation (support staff only).\"\"\"\r\nfrom flask import Blueprint, abort, g, jsonify\r\n\r\nfrom .. import db\r\nfrom ..auth import login_required\r\n\r\nbp = Blueprint(\"admin\", __name__)\r\n\r\n"]
[9.235474, "o", "\r\n@bp.get(\"/api/admin/orgs\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef orgs():\r\n    if not g.identity.is_support:\r\n        abort(403)\r\n    rows = db.query_all(\"SELECT o.id, o.name, (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM files f WHERE f.org_id = o.id) AS file_count \"\r\n                        \"FROM orgs o ORDER BY o.name\")\r\n"]
[9.235532, "o", "    return jsonify(orgs=[{\"id\": r[\"id\"], \"name\": r[\"name\"], \"file_count\": r[\"file_count\"]} for r in rows])\r\n"]
[9.235751, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[9.23579, "o", "root@d4ccd7b6-ea4d-48a5-a845-5e95f7dffe6e:/app# "]
[9.564304, "i", "sed -n '1,420p' tests/test_api.py\n"]
[9.564528, "o", "sed -n '1,420p' tests/test_api.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[9.566263, "o", "\"\"\"Feature tests for docshare (run from /app: python -m pytest -q tests).\"\"\"\r\nimport base64\r\n\r\nimport pytest\r\n\r\nfrom docshare import seed\r\nfrom docshare.app import create_app\r\n\r\n\r\n@pytest.fixture()\r\ndef env(tmp_path):\r\n    path = tmp_path / \"test.db\"\r\n    summary = seed.build(str(path), seed.DEV_SPEC)\r\n    app = create_app(str(path))\r\n    app.config[\"TESTING\"] = True\r\n    return app.test_client(), summary\r\n\r\n"]
[9.566342, "o", "\r\ndef user(summary, email):\r\n    return next(u for u in summary[\"users\"] if u[\"email\"] == email)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef h(u, org_id=None):\r\n    headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {u['token']}\"}\r\n    if org_id:\r\n        headers[\"X-Org-Id\"] = org_id\r\n    return headers\r\n\r\n\r\ndef org_files(summary, org_id):\r\n"]
[9.566411, "o", "    return [f for f in summary[\"files\"] if f[\"org_id\"] == org_id]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef test_health(env):\r\n    client, _ = env\r\n    assert client.get(\"/api/health\").get_json() == {\"ok\": True}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef test_login_required(env):\r\n    client, s = env\r\n    assert client.get(\"/api/files\").status_code == 401\r\n    assert client.get(\"/api/files\", headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer nope\"}).status_code == 401\r\n\r\n\r\ndef test_member_lists_and_downloads_own_files(env):\r\n    client, s = env\r\n    ben = user(s, \"ben@haldenprice.example\")\r\n    r = client.get(\"/api/files\", headers=h(ben))\r\n    assert r.status_code == 200\r\n    ids = {f[\"id\"] for f in r.get_json()[\"files\"]}\r\n    assert ids == {f[\"id\"] for f in org_files(s, ben[\"home_org_id\"])}\r\n    f = org_files(s, ben[\"home_org_id\"])[0]\r\n    r = client.get(f\"/api/files/{f['id']}/download\", headers=h(ben))\r\n    assert r.status_code == 200 and len(r.data) == f[\"size\"]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef test_folders(env):\r\n    client, s = env\r\n"]
[9.566469, "o", "    ben = user(s, \"ben@haldenprice.example\")\r\n    folders = client.get(\"/api/folders\", headers=h(ben)).get_json()[\"folders\"]\r\n    assert folders and all(fo[\"org_id\"] == ben[\"home_org_id\"] for fo in folders)\r\n    r = client.get(f\"/api/folders/{folders[0]['id']}/files\", headers=h(ben))\r\n    assert r.status_code == 200\r\n    assert all(f[\"folder_id\"] == folders[0][\"id\"] for f in r.get_json()[\"files\"])\r\n\r\n\r\ndef test_share_link_round_trip(env):\r\n    client, s = env\r\n    dev = user(s, \"dev@marlowclinic.example\")\r\n    f = org_files(s, dev[\"home_org_id\"])[0]\r\n    r = client.post(f\"/api/files/{f['id']}/shares\", headers=h(dev))\r\n    assert r.status_code == 201\r\n    token = r.get_json()[\"token\"]\r\n    assert client.get(f\"/s/{token}\").status_code == 200\r\n    assert client.delete(f\"/api/shares/{token}\", headers=h(dev)).status_code == 204\r\n    assert client.get(f\"/s/{token}\").status_code == 404\r\n\r\n"]
[9.566508, "o", "\r\ndef test_org_switching(env):\r\n    client, s = env\r\n    grace = user(s, \"grace@okafor-consulting.example\")\r\n    second = next(o for o in grace[\"orgs\"] if o != grace[\"home_org_id\"])\r\n    me = client.get(\"/api/me\", headers=h(grace, second)).get_json()\r\n    assert me[\"active_org_id\"] == second and me[\"role\"] == \"org_admin\"\r\n    ids = {f[\"id\"] for f in client.get(\"/api/files\", headers=h(grace, second)).get_json()[\"files\"]}\r\n    assert ids == {f[\"id\"] for f in org_files(s, second)}\r\n\r\n\r\ndef test_support_reads_any_org_but_cannot_rename(env):\r\n    client, s = env\r\n    riley = user(s, \"riley@support.docshare.example\")\r\n    for org in s[\"orgs\"]:\r\n        f = org_files(s, org[\"id\"])[0]\r\n        assert client.get(f\"/api/files/{f['id']}\", headers=h(riley)).status_code == 200\r\n    f = s[\"files\"][0]\r\n    assert client.patch(f\"/api/files/{f['id']}\", json={\"name\": \"x.md\"}, headers=h(riley)).status_code in (403, 404)\r\n    assert client.get(\"/api/files\", headers=h(riley)).status_code == 400\r\n"]
[9.566586, "o", "    assert client.get(\"/api/admin/orgs\", headers=h(riley)).status_code == 200\r\n\r\n\r\ndef test_admin_rename_and_delete(env):\r\n    client, s = env\r\n    anna = user(s, \"anna@haldenprice.example\")\r\n    f1, f2 = org_files(s, anna[\"home_org_id\"])[:2]\r\n    r = client.patch(f\"/api/files/{f1['id']}\", json={\"name\": \"renamed.md\"}, headers=h(anna))\r\n    assert r.status_code == 200 and r.get_json()[\"name\"] == \"renamed.md\"\r\n    assert client.delete(f\"/api/files/{f2['id']}\", headers=h(anna)).status_code == 204\r\n    assert client.get(f\"/api/files/{f2['id']}\", headers=h(anna)).status_code in (403, 404)\r\n\r\n"]
[9.566653, "o", "\r\ndef test_export(env):\r\n    client, s = env\r\n    ben = user(s, \"ben@haldenprice.example\")\r\n    fs = org_files(s, ben[\"home_org_id\"])[:3]\r\n    r = client.post(\"/api/export\", json={\"file_ids\": [f[\"id\"] for f in fs]}, headers=h(ben))\r\n    assert r.status_code == 200\r\n    out = r.get_json()[\"files\"]\r\n    assert [x[\"id\"] for x in out] == [f[\"id\"] for f in fs]\r\n    assert all(len(base64.b64decode(x[\"content_b64\"])) == x[\"size\"] for x in out)\r\n"]
