[15.442149, "o", "     1\t# docshare API\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tdocshare serves the documents that the ingest worker stores in its SQLite database (uploads go through the ingest\r\n     4\tworker, not this API). Who may call what is in `PERMISSIONS.md`.\r\n     5\t\r\n     6\t## Running it\r\n     7\t```\r\n     8\tpython -m docshare.serve --db <path to the SQLite file> --port <port>\r\n     9\t```\r\n"]
[15.442192, "o", "    10\tThe service listens on 127.0.0.1, uses the database file given by `--db` (it must exist; the service never creates\r\n    11\tone) and keeps all its state there. `python -m docshare.seed --out <path>` builds a fresh development database.\r\n    12\t\r\n    13\t## Conventions\r\n    14\t- Logged-in requests send `Authorization: Bearer <token>`; `X-Org-Id: <organisation id>` chooses the active\r\n    15\t  organisation (`PERMISSIONS.md` section 2).\r\n    16\t- Request and response bodies are JSON unless stated. Errors are JSON `{\"error\": \"<code>\"}`.\r\n    17\t- Ids are UUID strings. Times are ISO 8601 strings in UTC, for example `2026-09-14T10:22:05Z`.\r\n    18\t\r\n    19\t## Objects\r\n    20\t**File**: `id`, `org_id`, `folder_id`, `name`, `mime_type`, `size` (bytes, integer), `uploaded_by` (user id),\r\n    21\t`created_at`.\r\n    22\t\r\n    23\t**Folder**: `id`, `org_id`, `name`.\r\n    24\t\r\n"]
[15.442224, "o", "    25\t## Endpoints\r\n    26\t| Method and path | Success | Body of a successful response |\r\n    27\t|---|---|---|\r\n    28\t| `GET /api/health` | 200 | `{\"ok\": true}`; no login |\r\n    29\t| `GET /api/me` | 200 | `{\"user\": {\"id\", \"email\", \"name\", \"is_support\"}, \"active_org_id\", \"role\", \"memberships\": [{\"org_id\", \"role\"}]}`; `active_org_id` is `null` and `role` is `\"support\"` for support without `X-Org-Id` |\r\n    30\t| `GET /api/files` | 200 | `{\"files\": [File, ...]}`: the files of the active organisation, sorted by name |\r\n    31\t| `GET /api/folders` | 200 | `{\"folders\": [Folder, ...]}`: the folders of the active organisation, sorted by name |\r\n    32\t| `GET /api/folders/<folder_id>/files` | 200 | `{\"folder\": Folder, \"files\": [File, ...]}`, files sorted by name |\r\n    33\t| `GET /api/files/<file_id>` | 200 | File |\r\n    34\t| `GET /api/files/<file_id>/download` | 200 | the file's bytes, with its `mime_type` as Content-Type and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=\"<name>\"` |\r\n    35\t| `GET /api/files/<file_id>/t"]
[15.442253, "o", "humb` | 200 | an `image/svg+xml` preview: the file name and the first lines of a text file |\r\n    36\t| `PATCH /api/files/<file_id>` with `{\"name\": \"<new name>\"}` | 200 | the updated File; the name must be 1 to 200 characters without `/`, else `400` |\r\n    37\t| `DELETE /api/files/<file_id>` | 204 | empty; the file and its share links are removed |\r\n    38\t| `POST /api/files/<file_id>/shares` | 201 | `{\"token\", \"url\", \"file_id\", \"created_at\"}`; `url` is `/s/<token>` |\r\n    39\t| `DELETE /api/shares/<token>` | 204 | empty; the link stops working |\r\n    40\t| `GET /s/<token>` | 200 | the file's bytes, like download; no login |\r\n    41\t| `POST /api/export` with `{\"file_ids\": [<id>, ...]}` (1 to 50 ids) | 200 | `{\"files\": [{\"id\", \"name\", \"mime_type\", \"size\", \"content_b64\"}, ...]}` in request order; `content_b64` is the file's bytes in standard base64 |\r\n    42\t| `GET /api/admin/orgs` | 200 | `{\"orgs\": [{\"id\", \"name\", \"file_count\"}, ...]}` sorted by name |\r\n    43\t\r\n    44\tMalformed bodies (for example a missing `name"]
[15.442275, "o", "`, or `file_ids` that is not a list of 1 to 50 strings) get `400`.\r\n    45\t\r\n    46\t## Database\r\n    47\tThe schema is in `docshare/db.py` (`SCHEMA`). Tables: `orgs`, `users`, `memberships`, `folders`, `files` (contents\r\n    48\tare stored in `files.content`), `shares` (`revoked_at` is set when a link is revoked).\r\n"]
[15.442513, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
